    \item Small harmonic modes constrain the allowed rotations to preserve physical symmetries.
    \item Moiré patterns emerge from the superposition, serving as the intuition for how discrete structures (particles) arise from a continuous geometric substrate.
\end{itemize}

\section{The Process of Unification: A Step-by-Step Walkthrough}
The unification of gravity and quantum mechanics proceeds through the following structural steps:

\subsection*{Step 1: Establishing the Underlying SU(2) Field}
The framework initializes on a discrete $3\times3\times3$ lattice where a single SU(2) field defines the rotation at each point. This field serves as the fundamental variable from which both metric geometry and gauge structures are derived.

\subsection*{Step 2: Emergence of Spacetime (The Gravity Sector)}
