\subsection*{Step 4: The Resolution Pivot (Unification of the Sectors)}
The sectors are unified via the Universal Winding Identity ($\mathcal{W}$), which identifies microscopic vibrational modes and macroscopic orbital windings as the same object. The Coarse-Graining Scale ($l_c$) acts as a "zoom dial":
\begin{itemize}[topsep=0pt,itemsep=2pt,parsep=2pt]
    \item High-frequency resolution reveals worldlines as rest mass and discrete quantum gates.
    \item Low-frequency resolution reveals worldlines as smooth curvature and relativistic motion.
\end{itemize}

\section{Unifying Physics as a Whole}
The process for unifying physics as a whole involves treating the entire universe as a projective Moiré pattern generated by the Universal Winding Action ($S_{SAT}$). By solving the Unified Blockwave Action, physical properties emerge from the integrated 4D history of worldlines rather than point-local definitions. Gauge groups $U(1)$, $SU(2)$, and $SU(3)$ are recovered as redundancies of topological binding classes ($Q=1, 2, 3$), while symmetries higher than $SU(3)$ are topologically forbidden by a $Z_3$ lock.

